{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TXPoDt9ohnNLMX1Ves9AcZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-961\"\n3\ttitle = \"Claude coordinator sessions and their sub-agents, nested agents included, are recorded once per invocation from their transcripts, under the usage ledger's invocation key\"\n4\tworkstream = \"process\"\n5\tsr_refs = [\"SR-222\"]\n6\tspecref = \"docs/plans/2026-10-11-review-churn/README.md#8-record-usage-for-every-model-call-sub-agents-included\"\n7\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n8\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n9\tpriority = 5\n10\tplanmode = \"single\"\n11\tneeds = [\"WI-960\"]\n12\t+++\n13\t\n14\t## Context\n15\t\n16\tReview-churn item 8, proposal steps 2 and 3, with revision 37's widening:\n17\tplanners, builders and reviewers may spawn sub-agents, so nested agents are\n18\tin scope (queue row P2, second half). This row is split from WI-800. It\n19\ttakes WI-800's ledger contract (one usage record per invocation, keyed by\n20\tinvocation id, appended once), not WI-800's store. WI-960 is the first half.\n21\t\n22\t**Size of the gap** (plan item 8, leg 3, counted once per message id):\n23\tbuilders were about 74% of the leg's Claude output, and all sub-agents about\n24\t80%. None of it is in the kit's records. The coordinator session itself\n25\t(attended, or a headless `claude -p` leg: `overnight_legs.py` launches it\n26\twith `--output-format text`, so no result usage is captured) is not recorded\n27\teither.\n28\t\n29\t**Where the data is: verified on this box, 2026-10-20** (Claude Code; the\n30\treads are in NOTES):\n31\t- A session's transcript is `~/.claude/projects/<cwd slug>/<session\n32\t  id>.jsonl`. Attended (`entrypoint` `claude-vscode`) and headless\n33\t  (`sdk-cli`) sessions both write there. The slug's drive-letter case\n34\t  varies (`c--Projects-...` and `C--Projects-...` are one directory on\n35\t  NTFS).\n36\t- Every sub-agent of that session, **depth 2 included**, is a flat file\n37\t  `<session id>/subagents/agent-<agentId>.jsonl` beside\n38\t  `agent-<agentId>.meta.json`. The meta names `agentType`, `description`,\n39\t  `toolUseId`, `spawnDepth` (1 or 2 observed: 462 and 22 metas), and, for\n40\t  depth 2, `parentAgentId`, the depth-1 agent in the same directory. A\n41\t  `model` key appears only when the spawner overrode it. No depth-3 agent\n42\t  was observed.\n43\t- Each assistant message's `usage` repeats across records: one depth-2\n44\t  transcript held 86 assistant records for 41 message ids. Count once per\n45\t  `message.id`.\n46\t- The parent's tool result for a sub-agent carries a `usage` that is **not**\n47\t  the sub-agent's total: one depth-1 agent's summary reported 633 output\n48\t  tokens against 53,412 summed over its 20 unique messages. The summary is\n49\t  never a source.\n50\t- A sub-agent's environment carries `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`, equal to its\n51\t  parent session's id.\n52\t- A session launched under a declared account home (`CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`,\n53\t  WI-798) writes under that home's `projects/`: the ADJUDICATOR home\n54\t  (`%APPDATA%/project-trajectory/accounts/ADJUDICATOR/projects/`) holds\n55\t  `C--Projects-ai-template` and lane slugs. `session_keep.account_home`'s\n56\t  docstring says \"the kit never reads, moves, copies or deletes what a\n57\t  provider writes there\". LLR-336 (approved) narrows that to \"provider\n58\t  authentication state is never read ...; Codex rollout telemetry is the\n59\t  LLR-267 exception\". So this row reads the ambient home only. Reading an\n60\t  account home's transcripts would need an LLR-336 exception like the codex\n61\t  one (NOTES, call C6).\n62\t\n63\t**Not verified** (the lane's first step, recorded in its decisions before\n64\tany coverage claim): whether a resumed session (`--resume`, or `SendMessage`\n65\tto a finished agent) appends to the same file or starts another; whether a\n66\t`claude -p --output-format json` result's usage includes its sub-agents\n67\t(plan step 3; if it does, a service-launched Claude call's sub-agents are\n68\talready counted and must not be counted again); and whether any depth-3\n69\tagent can exist.\n70\t\n71\t**Anchor.** SN-026 (approved) through SR-222 (approved, derived). SR-222\n72\tbinds the sessions the loop launches. A session the coordinator's own\n73\tharness or an agent's tool spawns is not launched by the kit, so the lane\n74\tdrafts one derived SR under SN-026, performance lens, with a TC per arm. In\n75\tcapability voice (ruling 5): \"every model session spent on the project's\n76\tcoordinated work, including sessions an agent spawns within its own session\n77\tat any nesting depth, is recorded once in the usage record, and a repeated\n78\tor resumed recording adds nothing\". Its LLR states the reader's refusal on\n79\tan unknown transcript shape.\n80\t\n81\t## Deliverables\n82\t\n83\t1. **The reader, in one adapter.** The transcript format belongs to Claude\n84\t   Code (plan item 8, \"Trade-off\"), so its reader lives beside the claude\n85\t   adapter in `session_adapters` and is the only code that knows the shape.\n86\t   For one session it yields the session itself and each sub-agent at any\n87\t   depth. Each comes with its identity (session id, agent id, parent agent\n88\t   id, depth, agent type), its model, its usage summed once per message id\n89\t   in the vocabulary SR-222 pins (`usage_record` keys, input inclusive of\n90\t   cache), the message ids counted, and its first and last timestamps.\n91\t   It refuses, naming the file and the field, on a record shape it does not\n92\t   know. It never skips one silently.\n93\t2. **The invocation identity and exactly-once.** The ledger contract's\n94\t   minimal part, carried here because WI-800's ledger does not exist yet:\n95\t   - Each ingested invocation's `invocation-id` is derived from its\n96\t     transcript identity (session id and agent id), not from `uuid4`.\n97\t   - The log records the message ids it counted, as a count and a cursor,\n98\t     the last message id. The cursor is a column of the log, no new carrier.\n99\t   - A second ingest over the same transcript records only messages after\n100\t     the recorded cursor (a resumed transcript) or nothing (a repeated\n101\t     close-out), reading the logs already recorded, committed and spooled.\n102\t   - Each log also carries a contribution key, immutable and bound to\n103\t     the message range it counted (the invocation identity with the\n104\t     first and last message ids counted), so a resumed transcript's\n105\t     later log is a second contribution to the same invocation, never\n106\t     a duplicate of the first.\n107\t   - WI-800's ledger folds each contribution once, keyed by its\n108\t     contribution key, into its invocation's total (WI-800's\n109\t     Done-when, amended at this row's filing).\n110\t3. **Recording through the service's writer.** Each ingested invocation is\n111\t   one session log written by `session_service.record`. It carries a role\n112\t   of its own (`SUBAGENT` for a sub-agent, `COORDINATOR` for the session\n113\t   itself; never `BUILD`, `REVIEW-A`, `REVIEW-B` or empty) and the standard\n114\t   `call_` log name. Run from the primary checkout at close-out, it\n115\t   therefore spools under WI-960's out-of-lane arm. The log body is a usage\n116\t   summary only, never the transcript: prompts and outputs stay out of\n117\t   tracked records (SR-176). The usage source is marked as read from a\n118\t   transcript (`usage-source`), not reported by a launch.\n119\t4. **The command and its place in the cycle.** One command ingests the\n120\t   current session (`CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`) or a named one, from the\n121\t   ambient home's `projects/` (account homes stay unread, per LLR-336,\n122\t   unless call C6 rules otherwise). The coordinator runs it at close-out\n123\t   (`coordinator-cycle` §6) and a headless leg at its end (§7). It skips the\n124\t   main transcript of a session the service already recorded, matched by\n125\t   the log's `session-id`, so an adjudicator call is not counted twice.\n126\t   Whether it skips that session's sub-agents follows the plan-step-3\n127\t   finding above.\n128\t5. **Records.** IF-245's contract body (the reader), the command's\n129\t   interface row, the derived SR, its LLR and TCs, and one RESYNC entry\n130\t   (a new adapter and command in shipped modules).\n131\t\n132\t## Trust\n133\t\n134\tIngested logs land where a gate reads session logs (`docs/iteration/`, via\n135\tthe spool and WI-800's harvest). This row's ruling keeps them out of every\n136\tgate. Written under [PROCESS.md §3, \"When a guard is owed\"](../../../../project-trajectory/PROCESS.md#3-traceability--anti-duplication).\n137\t\n138\t- **Producer:** the ingest command, through `session_service.record`. Its\n139\t  input is Claude Code's transcript files, which neither the kit nor the\n140\t  owner writes. Failed writes: a log spooled for some invocations and not\n141\t  others (killed mid-run), or a spool write that raises.\n142\t- **Consumers** of the logs it writes (grep; the list WI-960's Trust gives):\n143\t  `project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/verdict.py` (`session_log`,\n144\t  `review_logs`, `logged_rounds`, the integrator's verdict gate), which\n145\t  reads only `SESSION_LOG_RE` names; `project-trajectory/scripts/agent_common.py`\n146\t  `phase_draw_ordinal` (skips `call_`) and `next_session_number`;\n147\t  `project-trajectory/scripts/agent_brief.py` `last_build_family` (phase\n148\t  `BUILD` or empty only); this row's own exactly-once read; WI-800's\n149\t  harvest and ledger once built.\n150\t- **Ruling:**\n151\t  - The ingested logs carry no gate authority: a `call_` name and a role\n152\t    outside `BUILD`, `REVIEW-A`, `REVIEW-B` and empty, so no consumer above\n153\t    reads one as a round, a build or a draw.\n154\t  - A transcript that is absent: nothing recorded for it, and the command\n155\t    names it. Unreadable, or of an unknown shape: the command exits nonzero\n156\t    naming the file and field, and records nothing for that transcript. It\n157\t    never records a partial sum as complete.\n158\t  - A sub-agent whose meta is missing or malformed: refused the same way.\n159\t    A depth-2 agent whose `parentAgentId` names no agent in the directory:\n160\t    recorded with its parent unresolved and the command says so. Its usage\n161\t    is real and is never dropped.\n162\t  - A killed run is recovered by the next run through exactly-once\n163\t    (Deliverable 2): what was recorded is not repeated; what was not is\n164\t    recorded.\n165\t  - The cursor binds to the logs already recorded, committed or spooled.\n166\t    An unreadable earlier log: the command refuses, rather than re-count\n167\t    or skip.\n168\t- **The bound** (PROCESS.md §6): transcripts as Claude Code writes them\n169\t  under the ambient home. A hand-edited transcript, and a session run under\n170\t  a declared account home (the adjudicator's), are outside the promise\n171\t  unless call C6 widens it. The adjudicator's own calls are recorded by the\n172\t  service already.\n173\t\n174\t## Done-when\n175\t\n176\tEach named test fails on the code before the change.\n177\t- **The reader**, on fixtures cut from real transcripts (usage values kept,\n178\t  text removed): a session with one depth-1 and
